<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luca Signorelli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1450–<a href="/years/1523">1523</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luca Signorelli was an Italian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> painter from Cortona, known for his powerful nude figures. His greatest work is the fresco cycle of the Last Judgement and the end of the world in the San Brizio Chapel of Orvieto Cathedral, painted from 1499 to 1504, which influenced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michelangelo">Michelangelo</a>. He also worked in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistine-chapel">Sistine Chapel</a> and at Monte Oliveto Maggiore.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luca-signorelli.jpg" alt="Luca Signorelli" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Luca Signorelli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Signorelli,_Luca_-_selfportrait_alone.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
